abstract: >
  A machine-verified research package: two Lean 4 + Mathlib libraries that
  formalize the Choptuik critical gravitational collapse — the discretely
  self-similar critical solution, its single unstable mode λ₀ = 2.6745, the
  mass scaling law γ = 1/λ₀ with the proved bound |γ − 0.374| = 263/2674500 <
  10⁻³, and the echoing period Δ = 3.445452402 — together with the Septinial
  braking satellite: the 24-slot dial with k = 24 − 2 = 22 = b₂(K3), the
  chiral split 11 + 11, the symmetry cascade 48 → 4 → 2, the exhaustive
  PSL(2,7) / Klein-quartic {7,3} enumeration (168 elements, 179 subgroups,
  14 × S₄), and the exact parameter-free three-term record
  γ₃ = 1 − cos(2π/7) − π/1200 = 0.373892. Zero sorry, zero project axioms,
  axiom audit exit 0 across 95 audited headline declarations; a rational
  certificate bridge (spectrum / newton / scaling / interval) connects the
  Python twins to the Lean kernel; every figure, animation and data file is
  deterministic (seed 1993). A machine-verified wing of choptuik_ac_bc.
keywords:
